  },
  {
    "name": "notification_and_escalation_workflows",
    "category": "functionality",
    "value": "Urgent or high-risk cases should surface immediately for the assigned team and move into active follow-up status. If key information is missing, the record should be flagged as incomplete and remain visible until resolved or deferred. Alerts should escalate first to the assigned investigator or supervisor, then to broader response leadership if no action occurs within the policy-defined timeframe."
  },
